From: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 10:12:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v2] wifi: cfg80211: keep the MLD SSID until the last AP link stops

An AP MLD has a single SSID which all of its links share: struct
wireless_dev keeps it in wdev->u.ap.ssid, nl80211_start_ap() requires
every link to be started with the identical SSID, and GET_INTERFACE
reports it once per interface through NL80211_ATTR_SSID.

___cfg80211_stop_ap() however clears wdev->u.ap.ssid_len whenever a
single link is stopped (NL80211_CMD_STOP_AP with NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID,
or NL80211_CMD_REMOVE_LINK), even though the other links of the MLD keep
their beacon_interval and chandef and keep beaconing. From that point on
GET_INTERFACE omits NL80211_ATTR_SSID for the MLD until a link is started
again, so to userspace the interface looks like it has no running AP.

This was observed with hostapd removing the 6 GHz link of three AP MLDs
on mac80211_hwsim: the Wi-Fi manager (pWHM) uses the shared SSID from
GET_INTERFACE as the liveness indicator of each affiliated AP and reported
all nine APs of the three MLDs as disabled while their 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz
links were still up and beaconing.

Use cfg80211_beaconing_iface_active() to clear the SSID only when no
valid link is still beaconing. The stopped link's beacon_interval is
already reset at this point, so non-MLO and last-link stops still clear
the SSID. A failed driver stop leaves the state untouched as before.

Internal whole-interface teardown, such as cfg80211_leave() on netdev
down, passes link_id -1 and stops each valid link in turn. Keep the SSID
until the last beaconing link stops successfully. An MLD STOP_AP request
without NL80211_ATTR_MLO_LINK_ID is rejected; it does not use that path.

Fixes: 7b0a0e3c3a88 ("wifi: cfg80211: do some rework towards MLO link APIs")
Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 net/wireless/ap.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/wireless/ap.c b/net/wireless/ap.c
index 9a9a870806f5..c935d2c31f3d 100644
--- a/net/wireless/ap.c
+++ b/net/wireless/ap.c
@@ -36,7 +36,9 @@ static int ___cfg80211_stop_ap(struct cfg80211_registered_device *rdev,
 		wdev->links[link_id].ap.beacon_interval = 0;
 		memset(&wdev->links[link_id].ap.chandef, 0,
 		       sizeof(wdev->links[link_id].ap.chandef));
-		wdev->u.ap.ssid_len = 0;
+		/* the SSID is shared by all links of an AP MLD */
+		if (!cfg80211_beaconing_iface_active(wdev))
+			wdev->u.ap.ssid_len = 0;
 		rdev_set_qos_map(rdev, dev, NULL);
 		if (notify)
 			nl80211_send_ap_stopped(wdev, link_id);
